<h2 id="p8-2-set-algebra-the-venn-diagram">2. Set algebra — the Venn diagram<a aria-label="Link to this section" class="anchor" href="#p8-2-set-algebra-the-venn-diagram">#</a></h2>
<p><code>Set</code> operations map directly onto the Venn picture. This is worth memorising because interviewers ask "how do you find the intersection of two lists?" and the answer is one method call.</p>
<figure class="fig-wrap">
<svg aria-label="Set operations as Venn diagrams" class="fig" role="img" viewbox="0 0 720 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
<g>
<circle class="venn-a" cx="80" cy="95" r="52"></circle>
<circle class="venn-a" cx="140" cy="95" r="52"></circle>
<text class="m" x="62" y="100">A</text><text class="m" x="152" y="100">B</text>
<text class="t ctr" x="110" y="182">Union</text>
<text class="m ctr" x="110" y="204">a.addAll(b)</text>
<text class="st ctr" x="110" y="224">everything in either</text>
</g>
<g>
<circle class="venn-o" cx="320" cy="95" r="52"></circle>
<circle class="venn-o" cx="380" cy="95" r="52"></circle>
<path class="venn-fill" d="M350 51 A52 52 0 0 0 350 139 A52 52 0 0 0 350 51 z"></path>
<text class="m" x="302" y="100">A</text><text class="m" x="392" y="100">B</text>
<text class="t ctr" x="350" y="182">Intersection</text>
<text class="m ctr" x="350" y="204">a.retainAll(b)</text>
<text class="st ctr" x="350" y="224">only what both hold</text>
</g>
<g>
<circle class="venn-o" cx="560" cy="95" r="52"></circle>
<circle class="venn-o" cx="620" cy="95" r="52"></circle>
<path class="venn-fill" d="M590 51 A52 52 0 0 0 590 139 A52 52 0 0 1 560 147 A52 52 0 0 1 560 43 A52 52 0 0 1 590 51 z"></path>
<text class="m" x="542" y="100">A</text><text class="m" x="632" y="100">B</text>
<text class="t ctr" x="590" y="182">Difference</text>
<text class="m ctr" x="590" y="204">a.removeAll(b)</text>
<text class="st ctr" x="590" y="224">in A but not B</text>
</g>
</svg>
<figcaption>All three mutate <code>a</code> in place and return a boolean, not a new set — copy first if you need the original.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="hl"><pre><span></span><code><span class="n">Set</span><span class="o">&lt;</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">a</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">new</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">HashSet</span><span class="o">&lt;&gt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">List</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">of</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"x"</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="s">"y"</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="s">"z"</span><span class="p">));</span>
<span class="n">Set</span><span class="o">&lt;</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">b</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">Set</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">of</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"y"</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="s">"z"</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="s">"w"</span><span class="p">);</span>

<span class="n">Set</span><span class="o">&lt;</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">union</span><span class="w">        </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">new</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">HashSet</span><span class="o">&lt;&gt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">a</span><span class="p">);</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">union</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">addAll</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">b</span><span class="p">);</span><span class="w">        </span><span class="c1">// x y z w</span>
<span class="n">Set</span><span class="o">&lt;</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">intersection</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">new</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">HashSet</span><span class="o">&lt;&gt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">a</span><span class="p">);</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">intersection</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">retainAll</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">b</span><span class="p">);</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="c1">// y z</span>
<span class="n">Set</span><span class="o">&lt;</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">difference</span><span class="w">   </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">new</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">HashSet</span><span class="o">&lt;&gt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">a</span><span class="p">);</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">difference</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">removeAll</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">b</span><span class="p">);</span><span class="w">   </span><span class="c1">// x</span>

<span class="c1">// symmetric difference (in one or the other, not both)</span>
<span class="n">Set</span><span class="o">&lt;</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">sym</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">new</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">HashSet</span><span class="o">&lt;&gt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">a</span><span class="p">);</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">sym</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">addAll</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">b</span><span class="p">);</span>
<span class="n">Set</span><span class="o">&lt;</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">both</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">new</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">HashSet</span><span class="o">&lt;&gt;</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">a</span><span class="p">);</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">both</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">retainAll</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">b</span><span class="p">);</span>
<span class="n">sym</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">removeAll</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">both</span><span class="p">);</span><span class="w">                                                    </span><span class="c1">// x w</span>
</code></pre></div>
<p>The stream equivalent, when you don't want to mutate:</p>
<div class="hl"><pre><span></span><code><span class="n">List</span><span class="o">&lt;</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">intersection</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">a</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">stream</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="na">filter</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">b</span><span class="p">::</span><span class="n">contains</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="na">toList</span><span class="p">();</span>
<span class="n">List</span><span class="o">&lt;</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">onlyInA</span><span class="w">      </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">a</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">stream</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="na">filter</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">x</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">!</span><span class="n">b</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">contains</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">x</span><span class="p">)).</span><span class="na">toList</span><span class="p">();</span>
</code></pre></div>
<p>⚠️ <code>filter(b::contains)</code> is O(1) per element only if <code>b</code> is a <strong>Set</strong>. If <code>b</code> is a <code>List</code>, this is O(n·m) — a classic performance bug in review.</p>
