<h3 id="p8-5-2-the-downstream-slot-where-groupingby-gets-powerful">5.2 The downstream slot — where groupingBy gets powerful<a aria-label="Link to this section" class="anchor" href="#p8-5-2-the-downstream-slot-where-groupingby-gets-powerful">#</a></h3>
<p>The second argument replaces <code>toList()</code> with any other collector, so each bucket collapses into whatever you want.</p>
<figure class="fig-wrap">
<svg aria-label="groupingBy downstream collector variations" class="fig" role="img" viewbox="0 0 720 210" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
<rect class="qbox" height="46" rx="5" width="200" x="14" y="14"></rect>
<text class="m ctr" x="114" y="34">groupingBy(dept, ??? )</text>
<text class="st ctr" x="114" y="52">same buckets, different fill</text>
<g class="leaf">
<rect height="30" rx="3" width="200" x="250" y="10"></rect>
<rect height="30" rx="3" width="200" x="250" y="46"></rect>
<rect height="30" rx="3" width="200" x="250" y="82"></rect>
