<h2 id="p8-7-rapid-self-test">7. Rapid self-test<a aria-label="Link to this section" class="anchor" href="#p8-7-rapid-self-test">#</a></h2>
<ol>
<li>Is <code>Map</code> a <code>Collection</code>?</li>
<li><code>groupingBy</code> vs <code>partitioningBy</code> — name the two real differences.</li>
<li>What does <code>toMap</code> do on a duplicate key? On a null value?</li>
<li>Why does <code>maxBy</code> return an <code>Optional</code> but <code>averagingInt</code> return a plain <code>Double</code>?</li>
<li>How do you unwrap that <code>Optional</code> inside a <code>groupingBy</code>?</li>
<li>Difference between <code>.filter(p).collect(groupingBy(k))</code> and <code>groupingBy(k, filtering(p, toList()))</code>?</li>
<li>Which map does <code>groupingBy</code> return, and how do you get a sorted one?</li>
<li>Set intersection in one method call?</li>
<li>Why is <code>list.stream().filter(otherList::contains)</code> a performance trap?</li>
<li>What does <code>distinct()</code> use to decide equality?</li>
<li>Which operations short-circuit, and which must buffer the whole stream?</li>
<li><code>teeing</code> — what problem does it solve?</li>
<li>Why is <code>stream.toList()</code> not the same as <code>collect(toList())</code>?</li>
<li>What happens if you reuse a stream?</li>
<li>When does <code>peek</code> not run?</li>
</ol>
<hr/>
<p><em>Answers to all fifteen are in the sections above, and in Part 1 §3 and Part 6 §A.</em></p></div></section>
